$f(x)=\left\{$\begin{array}{cc}$\frac{x^2-1}{x^2-2 x+1}$ ; & x>1 \\ $\frac{1}{2}$ \quad ; & x=1 \\ $\frac{x^2-1}{x^2+2 x-3}$ ; & x < 1\end{array}$\right.\because \quad x^2+3 x-x-3=x(x+3)-1(x+3)$
Lets Find
LHL, $\lim _{x \rightarrow 1^{-}} \frac{x^2-1}{x^2-2 x+1}$ and RHL, $\lim _{x \rightarrow 1^{+}} \frac{x^2-1}{x^2+2 x-3}\begin{aligned}
& \Rightarrow \lim _{x \rightarrow 1^{-}} \frac{(x-1)(x+1)}{(x-1)^2} \Rightarrow \lim _{x \rightarrow 1^{+}} \frac{(x-1)(x+1)}{(x+3)(x-1)} \\
& \Rightarrow \lim _{x \rightarrow 1^{-}} \frac{x+1}{x-1}=\infty \Rightarrow \lim _{x \rightarrow 1^{+}} \frac{x+1}{x+3}=\frac{2}{4}=\frac{1}{2}
\end{aligned}\therefore$ LHL $\neq f(1) \Rightarrow f(x)$ is not continuous at $x=1$
